{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"The is_reconfigured record changes the diagnosis. Node 3 reports holding an accepted StopSign (n3_reconfig 1) at accepted 37 and decided 37, while leader 4 reports no StopSign (n4_reconfig 0) at accepted 37 but decided 38. Node 3 therefore did not miss the AcceptStopSign: it holds the reconfiguration marker, and the leader is the node whose log lacks it and has moved past that position. The zero-divergence figure cannot be read as agreement at that position either: the harness builds each node's decided values from Decided(Value) entries only and compares the shorter of two prefixes, so a StopSign on one node and a value on another, and any length difference, are never compared. The update records the end state as a new fact, revises the question's hypothesis from a follower that missed the AcceptStopSign to a leader/follower split over the marker, and restates the interpretation: node 3's AcceptSync raised it to accepted 37 and the two later Decides were sequence-expected and clamped decided at 37, no AcceptStopSign is offered once the marker is accepted, and repeated Decides reuse a consumed sequence number. The promise record shows leader 4's prepare quorum did receive StopSign-bearing Promises in round 3 and its accepted index rose then, so the sync path that left it without the marker is the one remaining open link. The progress loss itself stays established and the agreement caveat is now explicit. No execution is requested.\"}"}}
